  "lineage": "Chilean adaptation of Colombian cumbia established in Santiago in the early 1960s by Luis Alberto Martínez's La Sonora Palacios and Los Vikings 5 — faster than its Colombian source at roughly 110-130 BPM, driven by electric organ or piano guajeo, two-trumpet-and-trombone brass riffs, timbales-and-congas kit playing and güiro on the offbeat, with unison chorus refrains; revived from the late 1990s as nueva cumbia chilena by Chico Trujillo and Juana Fe with punk-speed tempos and brass grit.",
